      "reason": "A1 lists four alternatives, including licensing, and separates the evidence question from the proposed solution. However, it states as constraints a test budget of €20,000 and a 12-week timeline, and a B2B portfolio of 'shipping, aircraft, military, marine'. None of these appears in the case or the sources. Invented numbers cap this dimension at 1. A1 also misses the key constraint the sources show: the FCC rule describes the PLB as a last-resort device used after other means are exhausted (acr-fr-purpose). It also misses that competitors McMurdo and Microwave Monolithics were approved at the same time (acr-gcn-three)."
